## What FBE.6c surfaced (foldback-reopening findings)

### BLOCKER-FBE6c.1 — Staging publish of `framework-only:main` deprives stranger clones of the `origin/framework-only` ref the bootstrap requires

The README's literal install (`git clone https://github.com/lukeivers/loam`
followed by `pip install -r install-from-source.txt` + `loam init
~/loam-workspace`) FAILS at step 3 because the staging publish writes
`framework-only` content into staging's `refs/heads/main`. Strangers
cloning staging see only `main` — there is no `framework-only` branch
ref published. The bootstrap's `_materialise_framework_only_branch`
helper looks for `refs/remotes/origin/framework-only` on the source
path; it doesn't exist on the stranger's staging clone (which has only
`origin/main`); the materialisation `update-ref` fail-softs (per design),
and the downstream `_clone_canonical` checkout step fails with the
BLOCKER hint "canonical must publish a 'framework-only' branch."

Reproducible just-now from staging URL `19422ed`:

```
$ git clone https://github.com/lukeivers/loam-staging.git /tmp/loam-stranger-fbe6c
$ cd /tmp/loam-stranger-fbe6c
$ git for-each-ref --format='%(refname) %(objectname:short)'
refs/heads/main 19422ed
refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 19422ed
refs/remotes/origin/main 19422ed
$ python3.13 -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
$ pip install -r install-from-source.txt   # → exit 0
$ loam --version   # → loam 0.1.0
$ loam init ~/loam-stranger-fbe6c-ws
[loam init] git checkout -B framework-only origin/framework-only in
/Users/lukeivers/loam-stranger-fbe6c-ws/framework failed (exit 128):
"fatal: 'origin/framework-only' is not a commit and a branch
'framework-only' cannot be created from it". Hint: canonical must
publish a 'framework-only' branch.
EXIT: 3
```

For comparison, the LOCAL canonical pos-v2 has both refs:
`refs/heads/framework-only` AND `refs/remotes/origin/framework-only`
(`framework-only` is a real local branch on the dev tree). FBE.10's
smoke + AC.FBE.6c.3's smoke both clone the LOCAL pos-v2 path
(`/Users/lukeivers/ivers-corp-pos-v2`), which has the ref —
so they passed. The bug only manifests when the source is a clone
of the PUBLIC URL.

This is the same SHAPE of bug FBE.6's BLOCKER-FBE6.1, FBE.6b's
BLOCKER-FBE6b.1, and FBE.9's BLOCKER-FBE9.1 were: documented
invocation works in the dev environment but fails for the stranger.
ODD §2.5 framing: the README's documented contract (clone → install
→ `loam init <ws>` works) is not satisfied by the actual code path
the README describes.

Fix shape (paths in priority order):

- **Path A (publish-side, recommended).** Push `framework-only:framework-only`
  instead of `framework-only:main` to staging; set staging's default
  branch to `framework-only` via `gh repo edit lukeivers/loam-staging
  --default-branch framework-only`. Strangers cloning staging then
  get `refs/heads/framework-only` + `refs/remotes/origin/
  framework-only` directly. Single-line change in the M12 publish-flip
  step's git push command + GitHub repo settings change.
- **Path B (publish-side, dual-ref).** Push BOTH `framework-only:main`
  AND `framework-only:framework-only` so strangers get both refs
  (`main` for the human-friendly default, `framework-only` for the
  bootstrap to resolve). Two-line change in the M12 publish step;
  preserves `main` as friendly browse default.
- **Path C (CLI-side, NOT recommended).** Make `_clone_canonical`
  fall through to the default branch when `framework-only` is absent.
  Weakens the named-synthetic-branch invariant; risky.
- **Path D (synth tool-default).** Make `pos-publish-framework-only`
  push to `framework-only:framework-only` by default. Same as Path A
  but at the tool-default level instead of the M12 invocation level.

Recommendation: Path A or Path B. Single-fence M12-or-publish-step
amendment; estimated 10-20 min wall-clock for the fix + a re-staging
push + a re-FBE.6d verification cycle.

